bg-brand-card\" href=\"/en/about\">About</a><a class=\"px-4 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium transition-all duration-200 text-slate-300 hover:text-white hover:bg-brand-card\" href=\"/en/contact\">Contact</a></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><a class=\"flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium text-slate-300 hover:text-white hover:bg-brand-card transition-all\" href=\"/ar/courses/mammography/mammography-equipment\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-globe w-4 h-4\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"></circle><path d=\"M12 2a14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0 20 14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0-20\"></path><path d=\"M2 12h20\"></path></svg><span class=\"hidden sm:inline\">العربية</span></a><button class=\"md:hidden p-2 rounded-lg text-slate-300 hover:text-white hover:bg-brand-card\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-menu w-5 h-5\"><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"12\" y2=\"12\"></line><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"6\" y2=\"6\"></line><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"18\" y2=\"18\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></nav><main class=\"flex-1\"><main dir=\"ltr\" class=\"min-h-screen py-12\"><div class=\"max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-slate-400 hover:text-brand-cyan mb-8 transition-colors\" href=\"/en/courses/mammography\"><span>?</span>Back to Course</a><article class=\"bg-brand-card border border-brand-border rounded-2xl p-8\"><div class=\"mb-6\"><span class=\"inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium bg-brand-cyan/10 text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/20\">Lesson</span></div><h1 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white mb-4\">Mammography Equipment</h1><p class=\"text-slate-400 mb-10\">Duration: <!-- -->20 minutes</p><div class=\"space-y-10\"><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4\">Introduction</h2><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Mammography systems are specifically designed to produce high-quality images of breast tissue using carefully controlled X-ray exposure. Understanding the major components of the equipment helps radiographers operate the system safely and obtain consistent diagnostic images.</p></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4\">Lesson Objectives</h2><div class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\"><div class=\"space-y-2\"><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Identify the major components of a mammography system.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Understand the function of the X-ray tube and breast support platform.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Recognize the purpose of the compression paddle.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Understand the role of the image receptor and acquisition system.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Recognize the importance of equipment checks and quality control.</p></div></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6\">Lesson Content</h2><div class=\"space-y-8\"><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">The Mammography System</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">A modern mammography unit consists of an X-ray tube, breast support platform, compression system, image receptor, positioning controls, and an image acquisition workstation. These components are designed to work together to produce detailed breast images.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">X-Ray Tube</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">The mammography X-ray tube is designed specifically for breast imaging. Its characteristics and exposure settings are optimized to provide suitable image contrast and spatial detail while keeping radiation exposure appropriately controlled.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Breast Support and Detector</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">The breast support platform holds the breast in position during imaging and incorporates the image receptor or detector. Correct positioning of the breast over the detector is essential for adequate anatomical coverage and image quality.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Compression Paddle</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">The compression paddle applies controlled pressure to the breast during image acquisition. Compression reduces tissue thickness and motion, separates overlapping structures, and contributes to consistent image quality.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Control and Acquisition System</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">The control system allows the radiographer to position the equipment, select appropriate exposure parameters, activate the examination, and review the acquired images. Modern digital systems also provide tools for image processing and quality assessment.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Equipment Quality Control</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Regular equipment checks and quality-control procedures are essential to ensure consistent performance. Radiographers should follow institutional quality-control programs and report equipment abnormalities according to established procedures.</p></div></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4\">Practical Example</h2><div class=\"bg-slate-900/40 border border-brand-border rounded-xl p-5\"><h3 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2\">Preparing the Mammography Unit</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Before an examination, the radiographer checks the mammography unit, confirms that the detector and compression system are functioning correctly, prepares the examination area, verifies patient information, and ensures that the equipment is ready for the required views.</p></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6\">Educational Images</h2><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\"><div class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-slate-900\"><img src=\"/assets/images/en/courses/Mammography/lesson-02/RB_MAM_L02_01_Mammography_Equipment.jpg\" alt=\"Digital Mammography Equipment &amp; Technology - 1\" class=\"w-full h-auto object-contain\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div><div class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-slate-900\"><img src=\"/assets/images/en/courses/Mammography/lesson-02/RB_MAM_L02_02_Compression_System.jpg\" alt=\"Digital Mammography Equipment &amp; Technology - 2\" class=\"w-full h-auto object-contain\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div><div class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-slate-900\"><img src=\"/assets/images/en/courses/Mammography/lesson-02/RB_MAM_L02_03_Image_Receptor_Digital_Imaging.jpg\" alt=\"Digital Mammography Equipment &amp; Technology - 3\" class=\"w-full h-auto object-contain\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4\">Common Mistakes</h2><div class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\"><div class=\"space-y-2\"><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Failing to perform required equipment checks.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Incorrect use of the compression system.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Poor positioning of the breast over the detector.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Selecting inappropriate exposure settings.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Ignoring equipment warnings or quality-control issues.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Failing to review acquired images before completing the examination.</p></div></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4\">Key Points</h2><div class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\"><div class=\"space-y-2\"><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Mammography systems are specifically designed for breast imaging.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->The X-ray tube produces the radiation required for image acquisition.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->The detector captures the transmitted X-rays and produces the digital image.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Compression improves tissue separation and reduces motion.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->The control system manages positioning, exposure, and image acquisition.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Quality-control procedures help maintain consistent equipment performance.</p></div></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4\">Takeaway</h2><div class=\"bg-brand-cyan/5 border border-brand-cyan/20 rounded-xl p-5\"><p class=\"text-slate-200 leading-8\">Understanding the mammography system and its components enables the radiographer to operate the equipment safely, position patients accurately, and produce consistent high-quality breast images.</p></div></section><section><p class=\"text-sm text-slate-500 leading-7\">This educational material is intended for learning and training purposes. It does not replace institutional protocols, professional training, clinical supervision, or applicable regulations.</p></section></div></article></div></main></main><footer class=\"mt-20 border-t border-brand-border bg-brand-dark\"><div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12\"><div class=\"bg-brand-card border border-brand-border rounded-2xl p-6\"><h3 class=\"text-white font-bold text-lg mb-4 text-center\">Available Payment Methods</h3><div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3\"><a href=\"https://wa.me/201115440838\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"flex flex-col items-center gap-2 p-4 rounded-xl border transition-all duration-300 hover:scale-105 bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 border-green-500/20\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\"